<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela is reported to have helped a drone strike that killed two Colombian soldiers in the Choco department, while a separate bomb attack near a military base killed four civilians, including an infant. President De la Espriella has ordered a renewed military offensive against dissident groups and increased aerial spraying following the Planadas bombing. The United Nations has renewed its mission in Colombia but excluded rural reform from its mandate. The government launched a broader offensive after seven attacks in six days. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxQV2JtLTUxR2RiTmlwNnljTDdjcDVjeHVkYVg0QktsS0tiUVhCOVBWMGNfejJTbG1MNUNOQ2lFZnhla3hGTDJ2eVFXRG14Yjk3am8wM3gyQ3E5b1ZGRzNoalJMQ0I1MXUxbDdUMkRJdmZucFNXWTFFTkZUN3Vpc0FVeWRiYzM0Sno1cS1JNTZrTG1BbmRiQk54Z3RuWllZOF96NjkyZkRoQzdvYWs?oc=5&quot;&gt;WSJ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxPb2p4akFMdUxTeWtlSkhaLXZBdXdyWkZLSFlPMm1EbDhGelRsUVlxV0N3cnYwZlZZemZiQWRrdTM0RVhhTG5PbDVVcy0xaVNEVW56d2FEYnA0ZGs2aEpnSFlmV2FuV3NHZ1F3N1pENC1Xa2JGeWJ3emo4eGY3ZkdHODEzcFMyUWYyRU9LQ1NjM1J1d29LaEpDMG9Tdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE5fWW05WWFRdXd6bFJjVU5RMko0dHdmalg4RWJQeF9HRnRyd1VPS2VrWWF0T0haQ2l2WGppRU5EVE1xZU1PbE1VeFVMWFVVdmhJMXVhQVlvdFV6OHpv?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxPTGtsRXlMUUFvSXVTSmRETkVHQnUwUm5GWDdILVZIZHZFSDB4X1M3ZDBrUnNLbnNwZ1hoSlJQREZGeklqY243ejdQUFRQTkc1SXBrX2hsallkeDJHQ3oyNF9mdjRUb093WGQ3emlrV3pYaUpTN3B1OFEwM245REFaLXRjdmxlajN3Wmw0LTRtZDNkTzA1WXd0cUhMemczLW8?oc=5&quot;&gt;PopTV Culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cU